  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-09-08T15:45:48.185Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Have you ever meet a stranger with avatar blocked? And do you wanted to see them properly, not that default unsacled dummy avatar? So you probably want to press \"Show Avatar\"... But you a bit of scared? What if its very poor, but I have weak hardware? What if it uses toxic materials and sounds? What if ...?\nFor situation like this I suggest new feature: \"peek avatar\": \n- Activates temporary, setting is not saved. When you or selected user leaves instance or changes avatar it resets back to disabled.\n- When activated on blocked user/avatar, game loads and shows avatar with all features disabled, except bones/meshes. Shaders are replaced.\n- Since shaders are blocked, it is fine to show perf-blocked avatar, may be up to twice performance limits.\n- If theres any way dozens of meshes with lots of materials and polygons, may be remove all the meshes and generate basic placeholder on humanoid bones to see proportions and size of a person. Or at least WHERE DAMN HEAD.\n- Emrgency \"Reset peeks\" in menu to block avatars back if something goes wrong. \n- \"Safe mode\" also triggers \"Reset peeks\".\nThis feature can be really helpful: when meeting starngers that you can not 100% trust, you just can turn on they avatar with limited features for a limited time.",
